{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-11-Jul-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "In an election, there were only two candidates. One of the candidates secured 44% of the votes and is defeated by the other candidate by 1440 votes. If there were no invalid votes. then the total number of votes polled is:", "options": [{"text": "15000", "added": false}, {"text": "12000", "added": false}, {"text": "14000", "added": false}, {"text": "13000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "Pomegranate juice contains 10% sugar solution and orange juice contains 30% sugar solution. What is the percentage of sugar solution in a mixture of two litres of pomegranate juice and three litres of orange juice?", "options": [{"text": "22%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "40%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "mixture-price", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Three cubes each of side 5 cm are joined end to end. The surface area of the resulting cuboid is:", "options": [{"text": "150 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "175 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "350 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "75 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A vertical pole of length 6 m casts a 4 m long shadow on the ground. At the same time, a tower casts a 28 m long shadow. Find the height of the tower.", "options": [{"text": "42 m", "added": false}, {"text": "32 m", "added": false}, {"text": "36 m", "added": false}, {"text": "48 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The sum of the digits of a two−digit number is 9. The number obtained by interchanging its digits exceeds the given number by 45, then the original number is:", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "factors-divisors", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "In ∆ DEW, AB∥ EW. If AD = 4 cm, DE = 12 cm and DW = 24 cm, then find the length of DB.", "options": [{"text": "7 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "6 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "9 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "In an election between two candidates, 30% voters did not cast their votes and 200 votes were declared invalid. The winner got 65% of the valid votes. If he won by 1200 votes, then find the total votes.", "options": [{"text": "9000", "added": false}, {"text": "6000", "added": false}, {"text": "7000", "added": false}, {"text": "8000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Which of the following is NOT true regarding a circle?", "options": [{"text": "The largest chord in a circle has a length twice its radius", "added": false}, {"text": "Given any three points in a plane, there is always a circle passing through these points", "added": false}, {"text": "The ratio of the perimeter and radius of a circle is always constant", "added": false}, {"text": "A triangle with vertices on a circle and one side as its diameter is a right-angled triangle", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "A and B are two stations 420 km apart. A train starts from A at 11 am and travels towards B at the speed of 70 kmph. Another train starts from B at 12 noon and travels towards A at the speed of 30 kmph. At what time do they meet?", "options": [{"text": "2 pm", "added": false}, {"text": "1.30 pm", "added": false}, {"text": "3.30 pm", "added": false}, {"text": "3 pm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Mira can complete a piece of work in 20 days, Nina in 30 days and Sima in 40 days. Mira and Sima worked together for 4 days and then Mira was replaced by Nina. In how many days, altogether, was the work completed?", "options": [{"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "Divide 25 into two parts such that 6 times of the larger part added to 4 times of the smaller part is equal to 130. Find the larger part.", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "On dividing a certain number by 459, we get 19 as remainder. What will be the remainder, when the same number is divided by 17?", "options": [{"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "What is the value of a so that the seven−digit number 4645a52 is divisible by 72?", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "60%", "added": false}, {"text": "90%", "added": false}, {"text": "47.4%", "added": false}, {"text": "9%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "Shyam’s income is 20% less than Ram’s. How much is Ram’s income more than Shyam’s in percentage terms?", "options": [{"text": "80%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "47.9", "added": false}, {"text": "37.0", "added": false}, {"text": "39.8", "added": false}, {"text": "40.0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "O is the centre of the circle. Its two chord AB and CD intersect each other at the point P (internally) within the circle. If AB = 22 cm, PB = 14 cm, CP = 8 cm, then find the value of the PD.", "options": [{"text": "14 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "11 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "22 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "12 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "If the area of a rhombus is 70 m2 and its height is 5 m, its perimeter is ________.", "options": [{"text": "56 m", "added": false}, {"text": "35 m", "added": false}, {"text": "64 m", "added": false}, {"text": "25 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}]}